A||N||7||Springtyme||Ever hear a loud tapping... (pics inside)||||1||
Z||000000||Springtyme||11-19-2001||12:42 PM||||all of the sudden for no reason when you're doin about 70 down the highway? Well, let me tell you if you do, pull over as soon as possible. It means your tire blew apart =( Here's what happened....<P>Eric got his 3800 installed and running pretty well and my dad wanted to see it. Well, he doesn't have his speedo working yet so I followed him in my fiero to keep his speed under 100  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Well we were doin about 85 and there were cops up ahead so we slowed down to about 60. Once we passed them I started to speed up again. I hit about 70 and kept it there. My friend Liz was in the car with me and we started laughin and jokin around how my car was so slow compared to erics. All of a sudden I hear LOUD banging sounds. I look in my rearview, see nothing. I look in my drivers side mirror and see my tire flapping around in the wheel well. "Oh sh*t!!"<BR>I quick pull over into the outside lane, cutting a truck off, but luckily he got over into the lane where I was, pulled onto the median and shut the car off. As calm as I can, I say to liz "get outta the car"<BR>I wait for the cars to go by and I get out. I take one look at it and slowly walk to the other side away from traffic, sit down in the grass and began to cry  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR>All in all it wasn't too bad, it could be alot worse, but my poor car... Here are pics from this morning with the donut on.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nov18$01.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nov18$02.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nov18$03.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nov18$04.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Nov18$05.jpg"> <P><BR>If anyone has parts they wanna donate or sell... I'm in need... =(||||reg||1
Z||000001||WhiteFieroBlur||11-19-2001||12:59 PM||||oh man that is terrible, the tire did all that damage? I have like a really slow leak in a used tire I got that I have to fill up about every week or so. I get scared that it might go flat on me. what secific parts do you need?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Springtyme||11-19-2001||01:04 PM||||I need an inner wheel well and the black trim (including marker lights) around the bumper on an 88 notchback, unless other makes/years would fit it... <P>Yeah, the tire did all that. Hard to believe. Liz and Eric both said they saw stuff flying in the air, neither of them can believe it came from my car...||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||11-19-2001||01:16 PM||||FYI - I had almost the exact same thing happen to my '88 about 8 weeks ago.  The center moulding between the driver's door and the rear fender well came loose, acted like a lathe against the left rear wheel.  Rubber came flying out against the fender well, inner fender shreded, bumper cover well scarred.<P>Insurance picked it up for my $50.00 ded and paid a GM dealer $870 for repairing the damage.  Inner fender well had to come from a "pre-owned" source.  No longer available from GM.<P>All in all:  New tire, refinish fender above tire, replace inner fender well, replace left moulding and refinish rear bumper cover.<P>Looks same as yours except I didn't need marker light but I needed the moulding forward of the wheel well.<P>Good luck.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||9
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||11-19-2001||01:34 PM||||You mean the black mess won't just buff off the paint? <P>It hasn't happened to me (knock on wood), so I don't know from experience...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||11-19-2001||05:12 PM||||Its really not as bad as it looks! New trim, a wheel well and all you have left is fixing your paint, maybe a few little other things. Im sure you can find all the parts you need in the Mall. Have you tried rubbing compound on the black marks? They "might" come out. If they dont maybe try wetsanding. If all else fails you just need a little paint job touch up.<P>Good luck!||||reg||1
